From f2e53d3839f846a44f5e6bd50f7ddb18886fe22b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: beau4201 <beau.ten.berge@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 23:24:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Vibrator: keep a valid frequency profile in the rounded
 calibration

withCoarseCalibration() built FrequencyProfile(resonant, null, null), which is
invalid by construction: it logged 'Invalid frequency profile received from HAL' for
every call and left getFrequencyProfile() null and the envelope effects reported as
unsupported although the hardware supports them. Keep the usable range (lowest and
highest frequency and resonant frequency to 10 Hz) and replace the measured curve
by a flat one at the maximum acceleration to 0.5 G; an empty profile is returned
unchanged. The rounding moves to a package-private VibratorCoarse so that a host
test can run it, and no longer turns an infinite value into Integer.MAX_VALUE.
---
 core/java/android/os/VibratorCoarse.java | 46 ++++++++++++++++++++++++
 core/java/android/os/VibratorInfo.java   | 32 ++++++++++++-----
 2 files changed, 69 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 core/java/android/os/VibratorCoarse.java

diff --git a/core/java/android/os/VibratorCoarse.java b/core/java/android/os/VibratorCoarse.java
new file mode 100644
index 000000000000..7dfc875a8a87
--- /dev/null
+++ b/core/java/android/os/VibratorCoarse.java
@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
